 "notes": "Answers: an address is 'street, city, ST ZIP', split into the form's street number, street name, city, state and ZIP boxes, with the suite as its own answer. The PDF has one From and one To box repeated on all seven days, so hours are written only when they're the same every day; 'Varies' leaves them for the applicant to write day by day. water 'Public: WSSC' ticks Public and WSSC. A partnership or LLC without workers' compensation insurance attaches the Commission's Certificate of Compliance instead. Left for the applicant: today's date, the fax boxes (the PDF uses one field for the facility's fax and the emergency contact's), the signature, and the whole payment page: Placetta never writes a card number. The checklist on page 1 is the county's. Mailed with the fee to Licensure & Regulatory Services, or faxed; the license fee ($200 to $525 by priority) is the person's.",
